cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Amenonuboco: Cyber Range as Code"
abstract: >-
  A manifest-driven dynamic provisioning platform for OT/ICS cyber ranges.
  From a single declarative manifest (topology, instrumentation,
  structuring, detection, and attack layers), Amenonuboco generates a
  fully instrumented Docker-based range: transparent traffic mirroring,
  a tshark-based real-time structuring pipeline, an auto-generated
  self-contained HTML network diagram, and an optional encrypted-traffic
  key-injection architecture (Dual-View Observation) for TLS-secured
  industrial protocols. Covers 15 critical infrastructure sectors and 13
  reusable protocol assets (Modbus/TCP, BACnet/IP, OPC UA, DNP3, SNMP,
  DICOM, HL7, SIP, EtherNet/IP, FINS, MQTT(S), SECS/GEM, MELSEC, PROFINET,
  EtherCAT), each verified with real client/server traffic captured and
  structured by tshark.
